<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Papinian</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Papinian was a Roman jurist of the late second and early third centuries CE, regarded as one of the greatest legal minds of the classical period. Alongside Gaius, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulpian">Ulpian</a> and Paulus he helped develop a sophisticated body of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-law">Roman law</a>. Their writings were later preserved in Justinian's Digest and form a lasting legacy of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/papinian.jpg" alt="Papinian" width="280" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rabax63 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aemilius_Paulus_Papinianus.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
